abstract: >-
  Twenty-nine years of regulatory half-hourly metering at New Zealand grid
  exit points measure a national power system's reactive character crossing
  from lagging to leading overnight, attribute the drift dominantly to the
  demand side, and identify a standing distributed-capacitance term
  accumulating behind consumer connections at about 230 VAr per connection
  over 2013-2025, with no detectable connection-independent residual, from a
  coefficient that crossed zero early in the 2010s. Includes both tiers of the
  paper with their LaTeX sources, and the full replication notebook suite
  computing every number from public data.
keywords:
  - reactive power
  - power factor
  - shunt capacitance
  - overvoltage
  - load modelling
  - power systems
notes: >-
  Two records. The paper (short version 11 pp, extended version 28 pp) is
  DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22238685 and is the one to cite. The data and code
  archive is DOI 10.5281/zenodo.21927098. Everything the author wrote is
  released under CC0 1.0; redistributed custodian data (Electricity Authority
  grid metering, Commerce Commission information disclosures) remains under
  its own CC BY 4.0.
